<title>EGYPT: Egypt state ups benchmark crude price for May.</title>
<headline>Egypt state ups benchmark crude price for May.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-owned Egyptian General Petroleum Corporation (EGPC) has raised by 10 cents the price of its benchmark Gulf of Suez blend against dated Brent for May, an EGPC official told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>The official said EGPC had also cut prices by five to 10 cents of three other crudes and left the remaining prices unchanged.</p>
<p>Following are details of May crude prices, all against Dated Brent (April diffrentials in brackets):</p>
<p>    Gulf of Suez	-$2.65 (-$2.75)</p>
<p>    Belayim	     -$3.80 (-$3.70)</p>
<p>    Ras Gharib	  -$4.40 (-$4.40)</p>
<p>    Ras Badran	  -$3.85 (-$3.85)</p>
<p>    Ras el-Behar	-$2.15 (-$2.10)</p>
<p>    Zeit Bay	    -$2.20 (-$2.15)</p>
<p>-- Miral Fahmy +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
